{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513136-tamers-of-nightmares-homebrew-left-handed-legacy","id":1513136,"title":"Tamers of Nightmares [Homebrew Left-Handed Legacy]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-28T17:03:24-07:00","id":1513136,"title":"Tamers of Nightmares [Homebrew Left-Handed Legacy]","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Legacy would probably be considered Left Handed in almost any Consilium or Assembly.<br /> <br /> The absolute most morally upstanding version of the Tamers of Nightmares is a Dark Knight style Batman: a vigilante that takes the law into their own hands in an attempt to scare villains straight, i.e. a criminal who does nothing to address the root causes of societal ills despite the power to do so.<br /> <br /> The majority of Tamers of Nightmares simply see a Mystery and pursue it for their own &quot;enlightenment,&quot; if the <span style=\"color:#000000\">M\u00e6re</span>\u200b have a home in the Pentacle it is likely with the Mysterium, in the Seers they're most at home under the Raptor, Exarch of Life.</span> <hr /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Tamers of Nightmares</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Humanity has always believed in monsters.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">And that\u2019s because monsters? They\u2019re real. There are things out there that go bump in the night, who tear human flesh from bone, stalk people down dark alleys at night.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">You know, you command them, and they do your bidding. Some you have bred yourself with magic, others you\u2019ve repurposed from natural animals and made stronger. And all have been enhanced with the stuff of humanity\u2019s very own nightmares.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Because those nightmares? They\u2019re also real, etched indelibly into the Temenos, the shared soul of humanity in a region called the Primordial Dream. And this shared fear is so deep seated and powerful it creates physical spaces within this otherwise non-physical world, spaces that connect between sites of profound fear and terror to other such locations based on the shared resonance. These are the Primordial Pathways, and they are the reason that monsters can disappear so quickly after the attack, or be in seemingly impossibly far away locations one after another, because human fear knows not mundane distance.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Navigating these Primordial Pathways is not without risk, however, an Awakened human is still a human, and those seeking to travel uninvited through the lairs of monsters best be prepared to handle themselves\u2026 until you\u2019ve become powerful enough to etch yourself as a Monster in humanity\u2019s collective consciousness and establish your own Lair in the Primordial Dream.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Origins</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Parentage:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Thyrsus</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Nicknames:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> M\u00e6res (Mares), Terror Bringers.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Background:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Those with an obsession for monsters, a fascination with the root causes of fear, or those who desire not just their enemies\u2019 demise, but their complete mental and emotional destruction.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Appearances:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Tamers of Nightmares either dress to intimidate, wearing clothing meant to evoke fear in onlookers, or to hide themselves from view, allowing their pet monsters to \u201cdo the talking.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Doctrine</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Mind 2, Intimidate 2, Animal Ken 2, and a predator, scavenger, or classically frightening animal with whom they have the Bonded condition.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Initiation</b>:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The prospective M\u00e6re must work with their animal to bring terror to a person. Those M\u00e6res worried about \u201cmorality\u201d or \u201cbeing a good person\u201d choose targets they believe deserve to be subject to a living nightmare, but the truth is they\u2019re scaring the everliving shit out of someone because they want to, there is no judge or jury involved.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Organization:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> M\u00e6res have no real organizational hierarchy: those with the largest Lairs have the biggest impact on the local Temenos and can assert some degree of influence over others, and M\u00e6res with a Verge attuned to Life can gain significant social currency by allowing their fellows to use it as a breeding ground for monsters. Unless two M\u00e6res are on opposite sides of the Pentacle/Seer conflict or involved in inter-Cabal/Pylon rivalries they will usually see each other as kindred spirits and will share information on Primordial Pathways.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Magic</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Ruling Arcanum:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Mind</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Yantras:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Places writ large in the local conscious as being places of terror (+2), the location of a recent (less than a week old) fear-related breaking point (+2), generally \u201cspooky\u201d locations (+1), terrifying images or sounds (+1), causing a fear-related breaking point (+3).</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Oblations:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> evoking feelings of fear, horror, or discomfort related to those emotions.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Theory:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Nightmares are an essential part of humanity with clear supernatural effects. By mastering these nightmares we master our own humanity and our magic.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Attainments</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">First: You Cannot Hide</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Initiation</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The first step in her studies of humanity\u2019s relationship to its own Fear, the M\u00e6re and any beast with whom she has the Bonded condition gain the ability to sense the exact location of anyone within sensory range with a fear related Condition or Tilt (e.g. Spooked, Beaten Down) by feeling the weft and weave of the local Primordial Dream. Any mundane attempts to hide from the Mage or her pets automatically fails, supernatural attempts to hide provoke a Clash of Wills on which the Mage enjoys a +4 duration bonus; this is a Mind effect. Additionally, the M\u00e6re and her pets can sense Irises to Primordial Pathways, if one is not in sensory range she instead feels a tug towards the nearest one, and can open the Primordial Pathway for a point of Mana and a Willpower; however, traversing Primordial Pathways without invitation is not without its own dangers (see below).</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Optional:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Life 1</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Within the Fear is knowledge, the M\u00e6re gains the ability to speak with all manner of frightening beasts as though under a persistent Speak with Beasts spell, though rather than being limited to a single species, the Mage can speak with any animal strongly associated with feelings of fear in the local Temenos and any with whom they have the Bonded condition.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Second: But You Should Run</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Mind 2, and either Intimidate 3 or Animal Ken 3</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">As a M\u00e6re\u2019s research expands, she quickly realizes that merely sensing fear is not enough, she must also measure the effects on the Primordial Dream that occur when fear is enhanced. As an instant action the M\u00e6re can cause a wave of supernatural fear to emanate from either herself or one of her bonded animals, enhancing the terror of anyone nearby. This Attainment cannot cause fear from nothing, but will inflict the Cowed or Demoralized Conditions on anyone already feeling fearful, if the subject already has one of those conditions (and it wasn\u2019t caused by a spell or Attainment) then instead inflict either Frightened or Beaten Down. This Attainment has potency equal to the M\u00e6re\u2019s dots in Mind, is Withstood by composure, and affects an area equivalent to a small warehouse or parking lot (large warehouse or parking lot at Mind 4).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Optional:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Life 2</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">By harnessing the results of the primary portion of this attainment the M\u00e6re fuels the power of her and her monstrous pets, against anyone experiencing a fear based condition both she and her pets enjoy 9-again on their Physical Attribute rolls and Social skill rolls affected by appearance against the target. If that Condition is Frightened or the target has the Beaten Down tilt they enjoy 8-again instead.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Third: So I Can Chase You</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Mind 3, both Intimidate and Animal Ken at 3 dots.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Through her research into the effects of fear on the Primordial Dream, the M\u00e6re can now create her own Lair, with its own Primordial Pathways. She gains a Lair rating based on her Mind dots (see the Lair table below) which dictates the number of Chambers that can be incorporated and the number of spells the Lair can support (spells equal to or under this limit do not count against spell control so long as they\u2019re contained wholly within the Lair), one of these Chambers, called the Heart Chamber, is unconnected to a physical location and forms in the Temenos purely from the Mage\u2019s own psyche.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Chambers can be created from any location at which a human suffered a fear-related breaking point within the last month, to do so the M\u00e6re spends a point of Mana, a point of Willpower (which does not add to the roll), and rolls her Gnosis + Mind, on a success the Chamber is incorporated into the Lair, on an exceptional success the M\u00e6re regains the spent Mana and Willpower, and on a failure the M\u00e6re cannot add the Chamber and cannot try again until another fear-related breaking point occurs. Incorporating a Chamber marks the location with the M\u00e6re\u2019s Signature Nimbus, and the M\u00e6re can open a Primordial Pathway to her Lair from any location bearing her Signature Nimbus.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">A stable Demense can be established in the Lair, but the only Soul Stones that can be used are the M\u00e6re\u2019s own (one soul stone is enough to cover an entire Chamber); other rare objects capable of creating Demenses may still be useable within the Lair.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Optional:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Life 3</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">With her Lair comes easier access to the stuff of humanity\u2019s terrors, and the ability to incorporate those traits into herself or her pets. After a scene of mystically manipulating either herself or one of her Bonded animals the M\u00e6re chooses a number of traits equal to her Life dots as though she had cast the spell Transform Life with normal size restrictions ignored, any Bonded animal can be affected. These changes last a day (a week at Life 4). </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fourth: Because My Pets Need Sport</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Mind 4 and Life 4, at least 2 Chambers incorporated into the Lair</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">With this Attainment the M\u00e6re has discovered how to allow Nightmares to be made flesh, drawing even more power out of the Primordial Dream. The M\u00e6re can fuse Goetia from the Primordial Dream with her bonded animals to create Manticores per the Manticore Companion merit (Deviant: the Renegades pg. 101) with the following changes: the dot rating of the Manticore is equal to the bound Goetia\u2019s rank, and the Goetia can assign its Attribute dots to raising the host animal\u2019s Attributes (Power dots can be assigned to Intelligence, Strength, or Presence; Finesse to Wits, Dexterity, or Manipulation; and Resistance to Resolve, Stamina, or Composure). The Goetia does not suffer Essence bleed while bound, and can spend essence on its Influences, but its Numina are replaced with Variations. Rank 2 and below Goetia can be forced into service, but Rank 3 through 5 Goetia must be convinced and can end the merge at any time (otherwise the merge is permanent). Rank 6+ Goetia are too powerful to be contained within the body of an animal. A M\u00e6re can have a number of Manticores equal to her dots in Life. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fifth: Before the True Monster Comes</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite:</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Mind 5, Life 5, Intimidate and Animal Ken 4, at least 4 Chambers incorporated into the Lair. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The culmination of her research, the M\u00e6re now gives birth to a creature of true Nightmare: their own Horror. The Horror uses the highest of the M\u00e6re\u2019s Intelligence, Strength, or Presence as its Power; the highest of Wits, Dexterity, or Manipulation as Finesse; and the highest of Resolve, Stamina, or Composure as Resistance. It then gains two additional points per Chamber in the Lair to assign to its Attributes. Its size can be up to the M\u00e6re\u2019s Gnosis, and the Horror can be a swarm. The Horror can freely use any Praxis the M\u00e6re knows, it uses the M\u00e6re\u2019s Gnosis + Arcanum rating to cast, cannot use yantras, and cannot contain Paradox (the M\u00e6re suffers the normal breaking point for releasing Paradox if released it\u2019s released by her Horror). The Horror is the M\u00e6re\u2019s soul, and the M\u00e6re is immune to any effects that would attempt to steal her soul; however, if the Horror dies the M\u00e6re immediately begins suffering the effects of the Thrall condition, the Horror reforms when the M\u00e6re gets a new soul and meets the prerequisites for this Attainment.</span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Lair</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Max Chambers</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Active Spells</span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">3</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">4</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">2</span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">4</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">5</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">3</span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">5</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">7</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">4</span></span></div></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> </span></span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Primordial Pathways, Chambers, Burrows, and Lairs</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Primordial Pathways can allow a M\u00e6re to travel anywhere in the world with human inhabitants, but the collective Fears of humanity are not safe by any means. Every time the M\u00e6re travels through a Primordial Pathway other than one to or from a Chamber incorporated into her Lair the M\u00e6re must roll Wits + Resolve with bonuses and/or penalties as outlined below.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Resolve</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana + 1 Willpower</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Action:</b> Instant</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Roll Results</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> the Primordial Pathway leads to the Lair of a hostile monster (represented by a Horde type Nightmare, Chronicles of Darkness pg. 143, a Rank 3+ Goetia immune to Mind magic, or a Beast from Beast: the Primordial). If the M\u00e6re attempts to escape a Chase ensues with the Lair\u2019s owner having the edge.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Failure:</b> the M\u00e6re gets lost, ending up in an unknown and potentially dangerous location and cannot attempt to open another Primordial Pathway for a Scene.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Success:</b> the Primordial Pathway opens and lasts for the M\u00e6re\u2019s Resolve in turns.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> the Primordial Pathway opens and lasts for the rest of the scene.</span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Modifier</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Situation</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">+3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The M\u00e6re has a Strong sympathetic connection to the destination.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">+2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The M\u00e6re has a Medium sympathetic connection to the destination.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">+1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The M\u00e6re has a Weak sympathetic connection to the destination.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">+0</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The M\u00e6re has been to the destination before, but does not have a sympathetic connection.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">-1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The M\u00e6re has scryed the destination.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">-2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The M\u00e6re has a picture or video of the destination.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">-3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The M\u00e6re has only heard of the destination or seen its location on a map.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">-5</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The M\u00e6re is travelling to a random destination.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">+2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">A powerful local Primordial Dream denizen has guaranteed safe passage.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">-3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The local Primordial Dream denizens are hostile to the M\u00e6re.</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">A Chamber\u2019s size is based on how large it loomed in the mind of the person suffering the breaking point, not the physical size of the location the breaking point occurred. A breaking point that ended in a failed roll produces a Chamber the size of a house, whereas a dramatic failure can produce a Chamber the size of a warehouse.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Burrows are what connect Chambers in a single Lair. The owner of a Lair and any of their guests can freely move between Chambers, anyone else must roll Intelligence + Resolve contested by the owner\u2019s Power + Resistance (or Gnosis + Mind for a M\u00e6re\u2019s Lair without a Horror). The owner of a Lair may also designate only certain Chambers as being for entry and/or egress (some put the entry in one chamber and the egress in another), with the only requirement being that every Chamber is connected to another by a Burrow.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Heart Chamber is the most important Chamber in a Lair, its destruction causes the entire Lair to collapse and need to be rebuilt, for this reason Heart Chambers are usually behind several other Chambers and well fortified.</span><br /> \u200b</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-28-2023, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T17:07:35-07:00","id":1513137,"title":"","content":"The Fangs of Mara must either fervently love or intensely hate these guys.<br /> <br /> By Animal Handling, I assume you mean Animal Ken? (Be careful about editing, though\u2026)<br /> <br /> EDIT: (Hope the God-Machine doesn\u2019t eat my post)<br /> <br /> If this is explicitly a crossover material between Mage and Beast, may I suggest using the Horrorspawn rules for the 4th Attainment, instead of Manticore rules for Deviant? (Granted, we can make an argument for using the latter for the former, or replacing both with a more generic or Mage-friendly system for purposes of this homebrew, but still.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-28-2023, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T17:18:49-07:00","id":1513138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513136-tamers-of-nightmares-homebrew-left-handed-legacy?p=1513137#post1513137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fangs of Mara must either fervently love or intensely hate these guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably see them as prime targets for bringing in to the Abyssal fold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By Animal Handling, I assume you mean Animal Ken? (Be careful about editing, though\u2026) </div> </div> </div>...Yes, yes I do, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T22:48:56-07:00","id":1513164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513136-tamers-of-nightmares-homebrew-left-handed-legacy?p=1513137#post1513137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: (Hope the God-Machine doesn\u2019t eat my post)<br /> <br /> If this is explicitly a crossover material between Mage and Beast, may I suggest using the Horrorspawn rules for the 4th Attainment, instead of Manticore rules for Deviant? (Granted, we can make an argument for using the latter for the former, or replacing both with a more generic or Mage-friendly system for purposes of this homebrew, but still.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This was developed for a pbp that wants to minimize reliance on the Beast rulebook, and there was also a specific request to avoid Dread Powers if at all possible, as they are too ST facing.<br /> <br /> There is no reason that anyone using this Legacy couldn't use the Horrorspawn creation rules, the Horrorspawn's potency would be based on the Goetia's rank, rather than being tied to Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T14:38:19-07:00","id":1513233,"title":"","content":"Rather than Left-Handed, they seem like a Legacy that would be popular with followers of the Raptor. Reducing a target to a paranoid mess, with the constant threat of being hunted down by monsters tailor made to destroy them. Testing people by stranding them in the Lair with Saw like tests. They very much seem like architects of horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T09:40:21-07:00","id":1514019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513136-tamers-of-nightmares-homebrew-left-handed-legacy?p=1513164#post1513164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was developed for a pbp that wants to minimize reliance on the Beast rulebook, and there was also a specific request to avoid Dread Powers if at all possible, as they are too ST facing.<br /> <br /> There is no reason that anyone using this Legacy couldn't use the Horrorspawn creation rules, the Horrorspawn's potency would be based on the Goetia's rank, rather than being tied to Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>It bugs me that it doesn\u2019t just use the Claim Manifestation rules, since Claiming is literally what\u2019s described. But the Mage core doesn\u2019t actually include Claim, and you kinda need Dread Powers to flesh (heh puns) Claimed out properly. <br /> <br /> Also, I feel like the heart chamber should explicitly replace the Mage\u2019s Oneiros, rather than just vaguely forming out of their psyche. <br /> <br /> I quite like the concept. The emphasis on Life/physical monsters is an approach I hadn\u2019t thought of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T11:39:20-07:00","id":1514030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1513136-tamers-of-nightmares-homebrew-left-handed-legacy?p=1514019#post1514019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It bugs me that it doesn\u2019t just use the Claim Manifestation rules, since Claiming is literally what\u2019s described. But the Mage core doesn\u2019t actually include Claim, and you kinda need Dread Powers to flesh (heh puns) Claimed out properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly rewrote the relevant parts of the Claiming rules.<br /> <br /> If someone used this Legacy in their game and wanted to use Dread Powers that would work, too.<br /> <br /> Basically, any rules for making supernaturally enhanced animals could work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I feel like the heart chamber should explicitly replace the Mage\u2019s Oneiros, rather than just vaguely forming out of their psyche. </div> </div> </div>That is an AWESOME idea, I just didn't think of it. It makes perfect sense for the Mage's Oneiros to be vaulted into the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> It does raise questions about where the Mage's own goetia go (Lair hazards?), and what happens to their daimon (does it exist normally until the fifth attainment, where it becomes a supercharged Horror?), but yeah, really cool thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I quite like the concept. The emphasis on Life/physical monsters is an approach I hadn\u2019t thought of. </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T12:19:05-07:00","id":1514034,"title":"","content":"If that was the case, what are the consequences of a Prelate summoning the Chamber with the Iron Door into the material ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}